sixaxis: recognise clone DS3 pads reporting "PS3 Controller"

get_pairing() matches a controller on vid, pid AND name:

	if (name && strcmp(name, devices[i].name))
		continue;

Many third-party DualShock 3 clones use Sony's 054c:0268 identifiers but
report the generic HID name "PS3 Controller", which is in neither table
entry ("Sony PLAYSTATION(R)3 Controller" and "SHANWAN PS3 GamePad").

The failure is completely silent. get_pairing() returns NULL, and
device_added() bails before its info() call, so bluetoothd logs nothing at
all -- the plugin appears to load and then ignore the pad. Everything else
looks correct while debugging: the hidraw node is created, HID_ID and
HID_NAME are present on the parent, udev broadcasts the add event, and the
adapter is up and default.

Add an entry for the generic name, alongside the existing SHANWAN clone
entry which was added for the same reason.

Observed on a BananaPi M2 Magic with a clone DS3:
  HID_ID=0003:0000054C:00000268
  HID_NAME=PS3 Controller

Signed-off-by: RetroBPI_M2M

--- a/profiles/input/sixaxis.h
+++ b/profiles/input/sixaxis.h
@@ -49,6 +49,22 @@
 			.type = CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS,
 		},
 		{
+			/*
+			 * Many third-party DS3 clones report the generic name
+			 * "PS3 Controller" while using Sony's 054c:0268 IDs. The
+			 * match below requires vid, pid AND name to agree, so such
+			 * pads are silently ignored: get_pairing() returns NULL and
+			 * device_added() returns without logging anything, which
+			 * makes it look as though the plugin never ran.
+			 */
+			.name = "PS3 Controller",
+			.source = 0x0002,
+			.vid = 0x054c,
+			.pid = 0x0268,
+			.version = 0x0000,
+			.type = CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS,
+		},
+		{
 			.name = "Navigation Controller",
 			.source = 0x0002,
 			.vid = 0x054c,
